Package: powerrules
Title: Power Rules for Balanced Between-Subjects Designs
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Carlisle", "Rainey", email = "crainey@fsu.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8728-4696"))
Description: Implements the rules from Rainey (2026) "Power Rules: Practical
    Advice for Computing Statistical Power" and its companion paper
    "Automating Power Analysis with Pilot Data" for balanced,
    between-subjects designs. Provides a pipeline interface
    (from_*() |> find_*()) for computing minimum detectable effects, power,
    and required sample sizes, with manuscript-ready output sentences.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/carlislerainey/powerrules,
    https://carlislerainey.github.io/powerrules/
BugReports: https://github.com/carlislerainey/powerrules/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
